{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-job-14-1","title":"Job 14:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Job entreats God for favour, by the shortness of life, and certainty of death. 7 He waits for his change. 16 By sin the creature is subject to corruption.</p>\n<p>born. 15:14; 25:4; Ps 51:5; Mt 11:11 of few days. Heb. short of days. 7:1,6; 9:25; Ge 47:9; Ps 39:5 full. 5:7; Ec 2:17,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-2","title":"Job 14:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>like. Ps 90:5-9; 92:7,12; 103:15,16; Isa 40:6-8; Jas 1:10,11; 4:14 1Pe 1:24 fleeth. 8:9; 9:25,26; 1Ch 29:15; Ps 102:11; 144:4; Ec 8:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-3","title":"Job 14:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>And dost. 7:17,18; 13:25; Ps 144:3 bringest. 9:19,20,32; 13:27; Ps 143:2; Ro 3:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-4","title":"Job 14:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Who can bring. Heb. Who will give. 15:14; 25:4-6; Ge 5:3; Ps 51:5; 90:5; Joh 3:6; Ro 5:12; 8:8,9 Eph 2:3 a clean. Lu 1:35</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-5","title":"Job 14:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>his days. 14; 7:1; 12:10; Ps 39:4; Da 5:26,30; 9:24; 11:36; Lu 12:20; Ac 17:26 Heb 9:27 the number. 21:21 thou hast. 23:13,14; Ps 104:9,29; Da 4:35; Re 1:18; 3:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-6","title":"Job 14:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Turn. 7:16,19; 10:20; Ps 39:13 rest. Heb. cease. as an hireling. 7:1,2; Mt 20:1-8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-7","title":"Job 14:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>that it will sprout. 14; 19:10; Isa 11:1; 27:6; Da 4:15,23-25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-8","title":"Job 14:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>die in the ground. Isa 26:19; Joh 12:24; 1Co 15:36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-9","title":"Job 14:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>and bring. Eze 17:3-10,22-24; 19:10; Ro 11:17-24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-10","title":"Job 14:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>wasteth away. Heb. is weakened, or, cut off. man. 3:11; 10:18; 11:20; 17:13-16; Ge 49:33; Mt 27:50; Ac 5:10 where is he. 12; 7:7-10; 19:26; Pr 14:32; Lu 16:22,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-11","title":"Job 14:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>the flood. 6:15-18; Jer 15:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-12","title":"Job 14:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>So man. 10:21,22; 30:23; Ec 3:19-21; 12:5 till the heavens. 19:25-27; Ps 102:26; Isa 51:6; 65:17; 66:22; Mt 24:35; Ac 3:21 Ro 8:20; 2Pe 3:7,10-13; Re 20:11; 21:1 awake. 3:13; 7:21; Isa 26:19; Da 12:2; Joh 11:11-13; Eph 5:14; 1Th 4:14,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-13","title":"Job 14:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>hide me. 3:17-19; Isa 57:1,2 until. Isa 12:1; 26:20,21 appoint me. Mr 13:32; Ac 1:7; 17:31 remember. Ge 8:1; Ps 106:4; Lu 23:42</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-14","title":"Job 14:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>shall he live. 19:25,26; Eze 37:1-14; Mt 22:29-32; Joh 5:28,29; Ac 26:8 1Co 15:42-44; 1Th 4:14-16; Re 20:13 all the days. 5; 7:1; 42:16; Ps 27:14; 40:1,2; La 3:25,26; Jas 5:7,8 will I wait. 13:15; 1Co 15:51,52; Php 3:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-15","title":"Job 14:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>shalt call. 13:22; Ps 50:4,5; 1Th 4:17; 1Jo 2:28 thou wilt have. 7:21; 10:3,8; Ps 138:8; 1Pe 4:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-16","title":"Job 14:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>thou numberest. 10:6,14; 13:27; 31:4; 33:11; 34:21; Ps 56:6; 139:1-4; Pr 5:21 Jer 32:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-17","title":"Job 14:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>sealed up. 21:19; De 32:34; Ho 13:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-18","title":"Job 14:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>the mountain. Ps 102:25,26; Isa 40:12; 41:15,16; 54:10; 64:1; Jer 4:24; Re 6:14 Re 8:8; 20:11 cometh to nought. Heb. fadeth. the rock. 18:4; Mt 27:51</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-19","title":"Job 14:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>The waters.Hence the proverb, \"Constant droppings make a hole in a stone.\"</p>\n<p>washest. Heb. overflowest. Ge 6:17; 7:21-23 destroyest. 19:10; 27:8; Ps 30:6,7; Eze 37:11; Lu 12:19,20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-20","title":"Job 14:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>prevailest. Ec 8:8 changest. 14; 2:12; La 4:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-21","title":"Job 14:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>he knoweth it not. 1Sa 4:20; Ps 39:6; Ec 2:18,19; 9:5; Isa 39:7,8; 63:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-14-22","title":"Job 14:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>his flesh. 19:20,22,26; 33:19-21 his soul. Pr 14:32; Lu 16:23,24</p>"}]}